139534554 17592186045417 true] [17592186425483 1074 "In the model, we have $\\frac{4}{6}$ multiplied by $3.$ This means that we need to make $3$ copies of the given fraction model.\n\n![](images/53/537b9211d3a5a35e8f4399b32337407cf89d6f8db131635be10e4c2c0b483830.png)\n\n \n\nSo, the missing picture is:\n\n![](images/f3/f3c802f3ae54c5aa0030cbb5fde6407d09fc2abb4ff4ca1b227909fbd80c6f27.png)" 13194139534554 17592186045417 true] [17592186425484 1068 #edb/ref 17592186425473 13194139534554 17592186045417 true] [17592186425484 1069 "q-60136" 13194139534554 17592186045417 true] [17592186425484 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534554 17592186045417 true] [17592186425484 1071 "![](images/f0/f06c991121e83d98fc0a0be73c8bad50f5f6ca0dd72a5e1648c99190b6263d73.png)\n\nUse the model above to calculate $3\\times \\frac{2}{8}.$" 13194139534554 17592186045417 true] [17592186425484 1072 #uuid "5f2b0524-ddd8-5adb-9825-3f8c1478c156" 13194139534554 17592186045417 true] [17592186425484 1074 "Since we need to multiply $\\frac{2}{8}$ by $3$, we repeat the fraction model $3$ times, as shown below.\n\n![](images/64/64485c4785783c04ef35908488163972a14785d3481e01d35d5490e411e26c74.png)\n\n \n\nThere are $3\\times 2=6$ shaded pieces in total. Therefore, \n\n$$\n3\\times \\frac{2}{8}=\\frac{6}{8}.\n$$" 13194139534554 17592186045417 true] [17592186425485 1068 #edb/ref 17592186425467 13194139534554 17592186045417 true] [17592186425485 1069 "q-60137" 13194139534554 17592186045417 true] [17592186425485 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534554 17592186045417 true] [17592186425485 1071 "![](images/b7/b75af537e5b32e5c9f17a819456d9cf2def508d1396bc93db074b7be44174646.png)\n\nUse the model above to calculate $3\\times \\frac{6}{16}.$" 13194139534554 17592186045417 true] [17592186425485 1072 #uuid "61e81fa7-42d5-567d-9362-7289c50d8428" 13194139534554 17592186045417 true] [17592186425485 1074 "Since we need to multiply $\\frac{6}{16}$ by $3$, we repeat the fraction model $3$ times, as shown below.\n\n![]