a2d63a1b31b169.png)\n\nThe shape on the left has $2$ shaded pieces, and the shape on the right has $8$ shaded pieces. So the number of shaded pieces has increased by a factor of $4.$\n\nTherefore, the multiplication problem shown is\n\n$$\n\\frac{2}{12}\\times 4=\\frac{8}{12}.\n$$\n\nSo, the missing number is $4.$" 13194139534554 17592186045417 true] [17592186425488 1068 #edb/ref 17592186425470 13194139534554 17592186045417 true] [17592186425488 1069 "q-192898" 13194139534554 17592186045417 true] [17592186425488 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534554 17592186045417 true] [17592186425488 1071 "![](images/f5/f5a61d6fa9f502dd21922b33d37b4cae7628f085f280ccb62a55cdde047d2c72.png)\n\nUsing the model above, express the following multiplication problem as a fraction:\n\n$\\frac{11}{12}\\times 2=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139534554 17592186045417 true] [17592186425488 1072 #uuid "861d93c7-2154-556c-a270-67d39e61a0df" 13194139534554 17592186045417 true] [17592186425488 1074 "Since we need to multiply $\\frac{11}{12}$ by $2$, we repeat the fraction model $2$ times, as shown below.\n\n![](images/e8/e8c59fe9adfedd533dcefb93fc62c9d9e911d63f8140a656537143ff2f8f2ae3.png)\n\n \n\nThere are $11\\times 2=22$ shaded pieces in total. Therefore, \n\n$$\n\\frac{11}{12}\\times 2=\\frac{22}{12}.\n$$" 13194139534554 17592186045417 true] [17592186425489 1068 #edb/ref 17592186425469 13194139534554 17592186045417 true] [17592186425489 1069 "q-60155" 13194139534554 17592186045417 true] [17592186425489 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534554 17592186045417 true] [17592186425489 1071 "![](images/98/9806837d4368cc36d604d796e6f0ccbc038813ed4d46e1afdbfd294709681d7a.png)\n\nUse the model above to calculate $\\frac{5}{6}\\times 2.$" 13194139534554 17592186045417 true] [17592186425489 1072 #uuid "a32733db-301b-58ed-82f6-69416a1d7088" 13194139534554 17592186045417 true] [17592186425489 1074 "Since we need to multiply $\\frac{5}{6}$ by $2$, we repeat the fraction model $2$ times, as shown below.\n\n![]